# the leading word of the "next to last" idiom (== "second-to-last", -2).
# Deliberately a SEPARATE table from marker_next.voc's REL_MARKER "next"
# (which shifts a whole scope by +1) -- "next to last" is not "next" plus
# "last" composing an offset, it is one fixed idiom meaning -2, and reusing
# REL_MARKER here would let the two collide.
next
